%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ea1fbb0ab59d4c84a59e909f29a5c4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day0
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: DontCallMe::DontCallMe.Data.DayData
  day: 0
  tutorial: 1
  dateLabel: Monday, 5 October
  weekday: Mon
  shortLabel: "Day 0 \xB7 Mon 5 Oct"
  place: Mangwon-dong, Seoul
  startTime: 14:10
  intro: 'A holiday Monday, your first autumn living on your own. This first call
    is practice: the yellow note shows you every place worth checking.'
  ringDelay: 7
  variants:
  - id: scam
    scenario: gas
    intro: 
    conversation: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a20345f45459944ebb5a73b0bccd2c80, type: 2}
    phone: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 93e737c48ff9240929f0678987855624, type: 2}
    room: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 412b533086ac0452d8c81010d6ff3218, type: 2}
    directory: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 56217da0c23fa4c80943a778fa833a70, type: 2}
    clues:
    - id: paper
      text: 'Today''s paper warns about exactly this: callers who say a bill is unpaid
        and want a transfer.'
      where: the newspaper on the desk
      guide: Every morning's paper warns about the trick going round. Click the newspaper
        on the desk.
      when:
      - kind: 0
        target: Newspaper
    - id: caller_number
      text: Her number is a prepaid phone opened three days ago, with four scam reports.
        It is not the gas company's.
      where: "Computer \u2192 Check a phone number"
      guide: The computer shows who really owns a number. Click the glowing laptop,
        then click her number under Check a phone number.
      when:
      - kind: 2
        target: 010-7359-2046
    - id: account_owner
      text: The "collection account" belongs to a private person, HAN SUNGMIN, not
        to Mapo City Gas.
      where: "Computer \u2192 Check a bank account"
      guide: The computer shows whose account it is, too. Click the laptop, choose
        Check a bank account, then click the account she gave you.
      when:
      - kind: 2
        target: 620-339-104772
      - kind: 3
        target: 620-339-104772
    - id: bill
      text: The gas bill in your drawer is stamped PAID (auto-pay, 28 September),
        and the company's real number on it is 02-555-0181.
      where: "Desk drawer \u2192 Gas bill"
      guide: Your own papers are in the desk drawer. Open it and find the gas bill.
      when:
      - kind: 1
        target: "Gas bill \xB7 September"
    - id: calendar
      text: Your calendar says today is a public holiday. Offices are closed, yet
        "the gas company" is calling.
      where: the calendar on the wall
      guide: The calendar on the wall shows what day it is and what you wrote down.
        Click it.
      when:
      - kind: 0
        target: Calendar
    - id: bank
      text: Your bank history shows 18,420 won went to Mapo City Gas on 28 September.
        The bill is paid.
      where: "Phone \u2192 Nuri Bank"
      guide: Your bank app shows what really left your account. On the phone, press
        Apps, then open Nuri Bank.
      when:
      - kind: 5
        target: 
    - id: chat
      text: 'In the residents'' chat the landlord warns everyone: the gas company
        never phones for money.'
      where: "Chats \u2192 Mangwon Heights residents"
      guide: People you know write to you themselves. Go back to Apps, open Chats
        and read the residents' chat.
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: villa
    - id: contacts
      text: The caller is not in your contacts. A number you saved would show its
        name when it rings.
      where: "Phone \u2192 Contacts"
      guide: 'A number you saved shows its name when it calls. Go back to Apps and
        open Contacts: is she there?'
      when:
      - kind: 6
        target: 
    papers:
    - outcome: 1
      headline: Holiday "gas bill" calls were fake
      subhead: Residents who checked their bill and their bank history hung up.
      body: 'A woman calling herself "Team Leader Baek" of Mapo City Gas''s billing
        team phoned residents of Mangwon-dong on Monday''s holiday. She said their
        September gas bill was unpaid, and that the gas would be shut off at five
        unless they transferred the money at once.


        Most of those called
        had already paid by automatic transfer. Police say the account she gave,
        Hanbit Bank 620-339-104772, is in the name of a man in his twenties who sold
        it to the ring. Anyone called by 010-7359-2046 can report it to 112 or the
        fraud hotline 1332.


        "We do not phone customers to collect bills,
        and our offices were closed for the holiday," Mapo City Gas said. "Our only
        number is 02-555-0181, the one printed on the bill."'
      verdictNote: You hung up. The bill had been paid on 28 September, and the account
        was a stranger's.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 5e14e13c5324c4c1d83b539fa6a79ace, type: 3}
    - outcome: 0
      headline: 'Paid twice: a gas bill that was never due'
      subhead: A Mangwon student transferred 18,420 won to a stranger on the holiday.
      body: 'A woman calling herself "Team Leader Baek" of Mapo City Gas''s billing
        team phoned residents of Mangwon-dong on Monday''s holiday. She said their
        September gas bill was unpaid, and that the gas would be shut off at five
        unless they transferred the money at once.


        A 22-year-old student
        sent the money. Her real bill had been paid by automatic transfer a week
        earlier; the 18,420 won went to an account in the name of Han Sungmin and
        was gone within minutes. "Small amounts are how they find out who will pay,"
        a police officer said. "The next call asks for more."


        "We do not
        phone customers to collect bills, and our offices were closed for the holiday,"
        Mapo City Gas said. "Our only number is 02-555-0181, the one printed on the
        bill."'
      verdictNote: The bill was already paid. The drawer, the bank app and the computer
        each said so.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: e21d49e3f110649a09c4220a746c65e6, type: 3}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: Fake "gas bill" calls go on through the holiday
      subhead: The gas stayed on. Few reported the number.
      body: 'A woman calling herself "Team Leader Baek" of Mapo City Gas''s billing
        team phoned residents of Mangwon-dong on Monday''s holiday. She said their
        September gas bill was unpaid, and that the gas would be shut off at five
        unless they transferred the money at once.


        Five o''clock came and
        went, and nobody''s gas was shut off. Police say the caller kept dialling
        until the evening, and ask anyone called by 010-7359-2046 to report it to
        112 or the fraud hotline 1332.


        "We do not phone customers to collect
        bills, and our offices were closed for the holiday," Mapo City Gas said.
        "Our only number is 02-555-0181, the one printed on the bill."'
      verdictNote: Nothing was sent, but you never gave an answer. Check, then hang
        up yourself.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 8f6fcd17512b24467ae721f194afb84e, type: 3}
    ruleTitle: Check before you pay
    rule: A caller's story is only a story. The number, the account, your own papers,
      your calendar, your bank and your chats tell you what is true. Check them,
      then decide.
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 6 Oct
  echoes: []
  nextDateLabel: Tuesday, 6 October
  builtWith: 8
